[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Enable the mechanism driver in %%PREFIX%%/etc/neutron/plugins/ml2/ml2_conf.ini:

    [ml2]
    mechanism_drivers = bsdbridge

Map physical networks to trunk interfaces in
%%PREFIX%%/etc/neutron/bsdbridge_agent.ini, then enable the agents:

    sysrc neutron_bsdbridge_l2_agent_enable=YES
    sysrc neutron_bsdbridge_dhcp_agent_enable=YES
    sysrc neutron_bsdbridge_l3_agent_enable=YES

The L3 agent needs the router service plugin in
%%PREFIX%%/etc/neutron/neutron.conf:

    [DEFAULT]
    service_plugins = router

Host prerequisites for the L2 agent's security groups:

  - sysctl net.link.bridge.pfil_member=1
  - /etc/pf.conf must compose the per-port anchors with if-bound
    states:
        set state-policy if-bound
        ether anchor "l2-neutron/port/*"
        anchor "l2-neutron/port/*"

Do not use the catch-all DHCP setting in /etc/rc.conf:

    ifconfig_DEFAULT="SYNCDHCP"

It makes devd run dhclient on every tap and epair the agents create, so
the host solicits DHCP on tenant networks.  Configure the real NICs
explicitly instead:

    ifconfig_vtnet0="SYNCDHCP"
EOM
}
]
